# Isolated remote state

The backend bucket should already exist with versioning, encryption, and restricted access. Each environment uses a separate state key, so applying dev cannot alter prod.

## `backend-dev.hcl`

```hcl
bucket       = "example-terraform-state-123456789012"
key          = "webapp/dev/app-support.tfstate"
region       = "us-east-1"
encrypt      = true
use_lockfile = true
```

## `backend-prod.hcl`

```hcl
bucket       = "example-terraform-state-123456789012"
key          = "webapp/prod/app-support.tfstate"
region       = "us-east-1"
encrypt      = true
use_lockfile = true
```

## Deployment

```bash
# Dev
terraform init -reconfigure -backend-config=backend-dev.hcl
terraform plan  -var-file=environments/dev.tfvars
terraform apply -var-file=environments/dev.tfvars

