## Kubernetes service account annotation

Apply this through the Kubernetes/EKS delivery layer:

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: ServiceAccount
metadata:
  name: webapp
  namespace: app
  annotations:
    eks.amazonaws.com/role-arn: arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/webapp-prod-service-account
```

No database password is stored in Git or supplied through plaintext variables: RDS generates it and stores it in AWS Secrets Manager. The service-account role has resource-scoped S3 and Secrets Manager permissions rather than wildcard resources.
